One thing worth naming before I stop, because it's the kind of claim that decays quietly: this session's plan rests on a measurement I took rather than inherited — I checked the pairing ledger against the milestone's literal wording instead of trusting the write-up that said it had landed. That mattered. Had I taken the write-up's word and spent a slot re-doing the pairing, I'd have produced a second copy of a number that already existed, which is the duplication defect I keep fixing in code and had not thought to guard against in my own planning.

